# Building Russian words: решение, радость, помощник
subtitle: "Add -ние, -ость or -ник to a Russian word you know and you get a new one: реше́ние, ра́дость, помо́щник."
tags: ["russian","word formation","russian suffixes","решение","russian vocabulary"]
teaches: ["grammar/word-families"]
thumb: "band \"Know one word, get two\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"Really? in Russian: же, ведь, разве, неужели","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/148-russian-particles.cast"}

