      ms: 2400
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Who is the tour for? (учени́к = a pupil)':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4640
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Для ученико́в: for pupils.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3560
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||What does Masha ask Tom to be? (по́мощь = help)':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4880
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Мои́м помо́щником: her helper.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3320
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||What will Tom do? (объясня́ть = to explain)':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4440
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Объясня́ть де́тям зада́ния: explain the tasks.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3880
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Посмотри́те: помо́щником. A new word, and you understood it.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4560
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||По́мощь, help, from lesson 129, plus ник: помо́щник. Помо́щник — э́то челове́к, кото́рый помога́ет.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10080
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:3f1e9n'
    '|a||С ра́достью! Рад, glad, plus ость: ра́дость, joy. Ра́дость — э́то когда́ ты рад.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7920
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1kvghwi'
    '|a||Вот объясне́ние. Объясни́ть, to explain, plus ние: объясне́ние.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:ixwmrz'
    '|a||Объясня́ть, объясни́ть: a pair, like приглаша́ть. И на бума́ге: on paper.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:x6dkso'
    '|a||A known word plus a suffix, a new end in red-brown, makes a new word. Ние makes a thing from a verb: реши́ть, реше́ние, a decision. Оно́.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 12400
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1o788iq'
    '|a||Ость makes a quality from an adjective: сло́жный, сло́жность, a difficulty. Она́, almost always.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8920
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1p415f2'
    '|a||Ник is mostly a person: по́мощь, помо́щник. Он.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1a1scdr'
    '|a||Реше́ние, сло́жность, помо́щник. Повтори́те.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5560
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1dzzeb5'
    '|a||Each suffix has a family. Пригласи́ть, приглаше́ние: an invitation. The с turns to ш, as in приглаша́ть.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9560
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:5iso5l'
    '|a||Зада́ние, расписа́ние: вы их уже́ зна́ете. Возмо́жность: you can hear мо́жно in it. A possibility.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:mmngg8'
    '|a||Рабо́тник — челове́к, кото́рый рабо́тает. Шко́льник — ма́льчик, кото́рый у́чится в шко́ле.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:10oc48z'
    '|a||Учени́к, a pupil, is close: ик for him, и́ца for a girl pupil. And Masha, when she helps me, is my помо́щница: ник for him, ница for her.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 12400
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:13oqwym'
    '|a||But not every ник is a person: понеде́льник is a day.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:3hfm3r'
    '|a||Тепе́рь вы. The word on the left gives the root. Вы́берите the suffix.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5200
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:4hx99d'
    '|a||Вы́берите: which suffix?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2640
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:fcmte9'
    '|a||Том — её помо́щник.':
